{"id": "unknown-2026-07-18-004", "date": "2026-07-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam attracts registered FDI worth $34.6 bn in H1 2026", "content": "Vietnam attracted registered FDI worth $34.6 billion in H1 2026—up by 61 per cent YoY. \nDisbursed FDI capital totalled $13.03 billion—up by 11.2 per cent. \nNewly-registered capital surged by 87.2 per cent, while capital contributions and share purchases rose by 89.5 per cent. \nAdditional investment in existing projects rose by 23.5 per cent YoY, while manufacturing and processing was the largest recipient. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-attracts-registered-fdi-worth-34-6-bn-in-h1-2026-311857-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-18-005", "date": "2026-07-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU, G77, China reaffirm support for Bangladesh's LDC graduation", "content": "The EU and the Group of 77 and China recently reaffirmed their support for Bangladesh's efforts to ensure a smooth, sustainable and irreversible graduation from the LDC status.\nThe assurances came during meetings at the UN headquarters during the visit of Commerce Minister Khandakar Abdul Muktadir, who explained the logic behind the request for a three-year extension of the graduation preparatory period. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eu-g77-china-reaffirm-support-for-bangladesh-s-ldc-graduation-311853-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-18-006", "date": "2026-07-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s $7.3 bn MMF boom has a 90% supply problem", "content": "Bangladesh exported $7.33 billion of selected MMF apparel in 2025, but imported $3.07 billion of MMF inputs, with China, India and Taiwan supplying 90.0 per cent. \nWoven fabrics accounted for 66.1 per cent of imports, highlighting reliance on upstream textile imports. \nFuture competitiveness depends on expanding domestic yarn, fabric and finishing capabilities. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-7-3-bn-mmf-boom-has-a-90-supply-problem-311843-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-18-007", "date": "2026-07-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam wage body agrees to 7.8% average hike in regional minimum wage", "content": "After a second round of talks between representatives of employees, employers and the government, Vietnam’s National Wage Council recently agreed to raise the regional minimum wage by an average of 7.8 per cent from January 1, 2027. \nThe wage will now rise by between 310,000 VND (~$11.81) and 390,000 VND per month, depending on the region. \nThe proposal will be submitted to the government for approval. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-wage-body-agrees-to-7-8-average-hike-in-regional-minimum-wage-311860-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
